\section{Why a set and not a dosage}{

A dosage says how many alternate copies a sample has, not \strong{which} alternate. At a codon
carrying three independently arisen changes that is the whole question, so the state is the
allele set: \code{"C"}, \code{"G"}, or \code{"C + G"} for a mixed infection carrying both. A sample with no
call is \code{NA} and is left out of every stratum downstream.
